# Jira CSV Format Reference

Specification for generating Jira-compatible bulk import CSV files.

---

## Standard Column Headers

Use EXACTLY these names (Jira auto-maps them on import):

```
Issue Type, Summary, Description, Epic Name, Epic Link,
Priority, Story Points, Labels, Fix Version/s,
Acceptance Criteria, Component/s, Reporter
```

---

## Column Rules

| Column | Epic Row | Story Row | Notes |
|--------|----------|-----------|-------|
| Issue Type | `Epic` | `Story` | Case-sensitive |
| Summary | Epic display name | `[FR-001] Short title` | Keep under 255 chars |
| Description | Empty | Full user story text | Plain text; no markdown |
| Epic Name | The epic's name | **Empty** | Used to create the Epic |
| Epic Link | **Empty** | Must match Epic Name exactly | Links story to epic |
| Priority | High/Medium/Low | High/Medium/Low | |
| Story Points | Empty | Integer (Fibonacci) | |
| Labels | `phase-1,module` | `phase-1,module` | Comma-separated, no spaces |
| Fix Version/s | Empty | Sprint name | e.g. `Phase 1` or `Sprint 1` |
| Acceptance Criteria | Empty | AC text | Plain text |
| Component/s | Component name | Component name | Must exist in project |
| Reporter | Author name | Author name | Must be valid Jira user |

---

## Epic / Story Linking Rule

Jira CSV import links Stories to Epics by matching the Story's `Epic Link` value
to an Epic's `Epic Name` value **within the same import file**.

```
Row 1: Issue Type=Epic,   Epic Name="Member Registration",  Epic Link=""
Row 2: Issue Type=Story,  Epic Name="",  Epic Link="Member Registration"
Row 3: Issue Type=Story,  Epic Name="",  Epic Link="Member Registration"
```

⚠️ Epic Name must be unique across the file.
⚠️ Epic Link must match Epic Name exactly (case-sensitive).

---

## Encoding & Format Rules

- UTF-8 encoding (handles Thai ฿, special chars)
- Wrap cells containing commas in double quotes: `"text, with comma"`
- Escape internal double-quotes by doubling: `"She said ""hello"""`
- No trailing commas
- One row per ticket (no merged cells)

